# LIBRARY: own
# A step down from a count that is not zero is a count: nothing is asked (f1). Any other step of an exact integer round a cycle of calls is guarded in a specialized version of the body, and the generic version behind it takes what is no int32: the second step of a round asks nothing (f5).
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: code f1:Body
# CHECK-NEXT: frame 0
# CHECK: b0(v0: int[0, 2147483647] @Int32
# CHECK: Sub {{*}} form=Integers
# CHECK: StrictEq
# CHECK: Sub {{*}} form=Integers
# CHECK: CallDirect {{*}} function=f1
# RUN(COUNTS): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# COUNTS-NOT: form=CheckedIntegers
# RUN(GUARDED): walk f5 mechanisms=all
# GUARDED: code f5:Body
# GUARDED: TypeTest v0 testedType=int[-1, 2147483646]
# GUARDED: Add {{*}} form=Integers
# GUARDED: StrictEq
# GUARDED: Add {{*}} form=Integers
# GUARDED: form=CheckedIntegers
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# ANSWERS: true true -3 2147483646 -2147483651 -9007199254740992 9007199254740991
# ANSWERS-NEXT: false false true
# ANSWERS-NEXT: exited with 0
